mode: "100644"
text: "# Triage & Severity\n\nThe first move in any negative moment is **not** to respond — it's to **confirm the facts and judge\nhow serious this actually is.** Most negative attention isn't a crisis; some is. Getting this wrong in\neither direction is the main failure mode: overreacting to noise, or underreacting to a real one.\n\n> Re-verify platform specifics quarterly; the triage logic is durable.\n\n## Step 1: confirm the facts\n\nBefore any public word: **what actually happened?** Is the claim true, partly true, or false? Don't\nrespond to something you haven't verified — and never apologize for something unconfirmed. If you don't\nyet know, that's fine (the holding statement says you're investigating — see `the-response-playbook.md`).\n\n## Step 2: classify the situation\n\nDifferent situations need different responses, not one template:\n\n- **A single complaint / snark** → **not a crisis.** Routine engagement (→ `reply-and-comment-writer`):\n  reply calmly or ignore. Don't escalate.\n- **A legitimate complaint with traction** (a defective product, a bad interaction going semi-viral) →\n  service recovery + empathy; handle well before it grows.\n- **Misinformation / a false claim** → **correct the record with evidence**, don't apologize (see the\n  deepfake note below and `the-response-playbook.md`).\n- **A deepfake / synthetic outrage / coordinated attack** → AI-faked screenshots, bot-amplified\n  \"backlash.\" **Distinguish genuine dissatisfaction from a manufactured attack**; correct with evidence,\n  report it, get ahead of it, and escalate.\n- **An offensive / tone-deaf post of yours** → own it quickly and genuinely; don't get defensive.\n- **An outage / product failure** → transparency + timestamped updates + a real fix.\n- **A systemic crisis** (attacks your core values, exec/employee misstep, safety/legal issue) → full\n  response + escalation.\n\n## Step 3: rate severity (sets urgency + who's involved)\n\n- **Low** — isolated negativity, no real spread. **Community management + customer care** handle it\n  (`reply-and-comment-writer`, `engagement-routine`). No alarm.\n- **Medium** — gaining volume/velocity, a real grievance. **Align PR + support**, a measured public\n  response, monitor closely.\n- **High** — fast-spreading, reputational/values/legal exposure, or safety implications. **Legal review\n  + executive visibility + a controlled response.** Escalate to people (`escalation-pause-and-safety.md`).\n\n## Speed vs accuracy\n\nNegative sentiment can reach most of your audience **before a statement is drafted**, and algorithms\namplify trending negativity. So **acknowledge fast** — but **accuracy still governs** what you commit\nto. The resolution: a fast *acknowledgment* (\"we're aware and looking into it\") buys time without\nasserting unverified facts. (Full timing in `the-response-playbook.md`.)\n\n## Output of triage\n\nA one-line read: *\"This is a [type], severity [low/medium/high]; response = [route], escalate to\n[whom], pause the queue? [y/n].\"* Then proceed to the playbook — with a human in the loop.\n"
